Eloquent — fluent and persuasive in speaking or writing
Example: The speaker gave an eloquent speech.
Gratify — to give pleasure or satisfaction
Example: Helping others can gratify you deeply.
Hinder — to create difficulties or delay progress
Example: Heavy rain may hinder travel plans.
Impeccable — perfect, without mistakes
Example: Her dressing style is impeccable.
Jubilant — extremely joyful
Example: Fans were jubilant after the victory.
Keen — very eager or sharp
Example: He is keen to learn coding.
Lucid — clear and easy to understand
Example: The teacher gave a lucid explanation.
Modest — humble and not boastful
Example: Despite success, she remained modest.
Notion — an idea or belief
Example: I had no notion about the event.
Optimistic — hopeful and positive about the future
Example: She is optimistic about her career.
